---
const scale = [
  ["perhaps", "Maybe. The speaker is considering a possibility.", "Perhaps the key is in the drawer."],
  ["possibly", "It could happen or be true.", "She could possibly arrive early."],
  ["probably", "Likely, but not certain.", "They will probably win."],
  ["certainly", "Strong confidence.", "I will certainly help."],
  ["definitely", "Firm confidence or commitment.", "We will definitely attend."]
];
---

<div class="topic-sheet">
  <h1>Possibility - How sure is the speaker?</h1>
  <p>
    <strong>Perhaps, possibly, probably, certainly</strong> and <strong>definitely</strong> tell us how sure the speaker is. They are adverbs, not modal verbs. Both can change how certain a statement sounds.
  </p>
  <section class="summary-block summary-lilac">
    <h2>From less certain to more confident</h2>
    <table class="punct-table summary-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th class="th-feature" scope="col">Adverb</th>
          <th class="th-rule" scope="col">Usual meaning</th>
          <th class="th-example" scope="col">Example</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          scale.map(([word, meaning, example]) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{word}</th>
              <td>{meaning}</td>
              <td>{example}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>This is a rough guide, not a set of exact percentages. <em>Perhaps</em> and <em>possibly</em> often overlap. <em>Certainly</em> and <em>definitely</em> show confidence, but they cannot guarantee a future event.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="summary-block summary-sand">
    <h2>Swap the adverb and the certainty changes</h2>
    <p>“<strong>Perhaps</strong> the train is late.” The speaker is considering lateness as one possibility.</p>
    <p>“The train is <strong>probably</strong> late.” The speaker thinks lateness is likely.</p>
    <p>“The train is <strong>definitely</strong> late.” The speaker claims to be sure.</p>
    <p>Ask what evidence would make that certainty reasonable. If the board says <em>On time</em>, “The train is definitely late” is not well supported.</p>
  </section>
</div>
